{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-03T10:37:06.414Z","author":"pi-toolchain-glm-1103","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"9e1c18dd119f0404d66458ad","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-03T10:37:06.414Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-03T10:37:06.402Z","author":"pi-toolchain-glm-1103","text":"Root cause reproduced and fixed on the branch pin (@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28): readClosureItems copies bootstrap/schema into the reader unconditionally, and read-side SDK calls stopped recreating missing workflow schema files in pm-cli 2026.10.25 (GH-1568), so a tracker whose schema directory is absent now fails the copy with ENOENT and both previews refuse local_read_failed. Classification: production code relying on old CLI read-side backfill. Fix: copy the schema directory only when it exists in the owned bootstrap copy (mirroring the existing explicit settings repair); reads on the new CLI no longer need schema files. Both previously failing tests pass: node --test --test-name-pattern 'source isolation precedes SDK backfill' test/dependency-closure.test.ts and ...'source isolation precedes SDK scaffolding' test/ownership.test.ts."}]}],"before_hash":"6ae320424f295c23af6a1adda7e53100b29b2a79216c2eef9b6bd3561815d238","after_hash":"ea70a12ab13bc921155d11eb2c07b6bbc64ef12a08f502cdf78e4f1fcd5c3354","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7a81fbe4a6024b3306face6e7ee80ac189095f4c2cfecd7b8920811195cc728b"}
